@startuml KTOB_08_sequence_reading_journal
title KTOB - Start, Update, Reread and Journal
actor Reader
participant "Angular" as UI
participant "Spring API" as API
participant "Auth guard" as Guard
participant "Library / Journal" as Library
database "Supabase PostgreSQL" as DB
Reader -> UI : Select owned library entry
UI -> API : POST /library/{entryId}/experiences
API -> Guard : verify identity, entry ownership and archivedAt
alt Archived entry
 Guard --> API : owned but archived
 API --> UI : 409 LIBRARY_ENTRY_ARCHIVED; no mutation
else Active entry
 Guard --> API : owned and active
 alt New current reading or reread
 API -> Library : create CURRENTLY_READING experience
 Library -> DB : ensure no other open experience
 DB --> Library : new experience (history preserved)
else Explicit historical import
 API -> Library : validate historical flag and requested status
 Library -> DB : insert past experience, preserve existing
 DB --> Library : new historical experience
 end
Library --> API : experience
API --> UI : 201 experience
Reader -> UI : Update status / dates / progressPercent / rating
UI -> API : PATCH /experiences/{id}
API -> Guard : validate owner and active parent entry
API -> Library : validate transition, progressPercent 0..100 (integer),\n  rating 1..5 (half-steps), no conflicting open record
alt Transition invalid
 Library --> API : invalid transition
API --> UI : 422 invalid transition
else Transition valid
 Library -> DB : update selected experience only
 Library --> API : updated experience
API --> UI : 200 experience
end
opt Reader saves reflection
 Reader -> UI : Journal content + personalization exclusion
 UI -> API : POST /experiences/{id}/journal
 API -> Guard : check owner and active parent entry
 API -> Library : save with allowForPersonalization flag
 Library -> DB : insert note
 Library --> API : saved journal entry
API --> UI : 201 journal entry
end
opt Reader edits or deletes a journal entry
 UI -> API : PATCH or DELETE /journal/{journalId}
 API -> Guard : verify owner through experience and library entry
 API -> Library : reject archived parent; validate partial journal patch
 Library -> DB : update or delete this note only
 Library --> API : updated note or deleted
 API --> UI : 200 journal entry / 204 deleted
end
end
note over Library,DB
Every descendant write rechecks parent archivedAt; 409 if archived,
404 for non-owner. Historic owned GET remains available.
Rating is optional (1..5, 0.5 steps); progressPercent optional (0..100 integer).
Progress and status do not auto-update each other.
Library shelf is derived, not persisted as experience status.
Excluded notes never enter external AI context.
Parent entry is locked during writes to serialize with archive.
Terminal status stays immutable; rating/date metadata remains editable.
end note
@enduml
